(CEDAR EQUIPMENT TRUST | CASH MEMORANDUM CE-9 | 2026-09-01) Tj
T*
(This is a fictional closed trust, not a public investment offer. Amounts in the exercise) Tj
T*
(are thousands of CNY. Interest targets are accounting obligations for a period, not) Tj
T*
(guaranteed returns. A trustee fee cap and the reserve target are separate limits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX A | COLLECTION FILE INTAKE) Tj
T*
(The equipment servicer prepares a collection file from actual receipts and identifies the) Tj
T*
(asset reference for each entry. A lease invoice establishes a claim but does not establish) Tj
T*
(that cash has arrived. Staff compare the file with the relevant bank movements and retain) Tj
T*
(unmatched items for investigation. An unexplained difference is not filled with an) Tj
T*
(estimated receipt merely because the estimate would make the distribution worksheet) Tj
T*
(balance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The collector's note can describe a tenant's promise to pay, an equipment purchaser's) Tj
T*
(installment plan or a disputed charge. These notes are useful operational context. They) Tj
T*
(remain separate from completed receipts until the supporting movement is available and) Tj
T*
(matched. A customer who confirms a payment has been initiated may still have supplied only) Tj
T*
(a remittance instruction, rather than evidence that the trust has received usable funds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When an asset reference is missing, the receipt is held for identification under the) Tj
T*
(operational process. Review staff preserve the payer's message and the bank record while) Tj
T*
(asking the servicer to explain the association. They do not choose the asset with the most) Tj
T*
(overdue lease simply to improve a delinquency report. The completed file should allow) Tj
T*
(another analyst to reproduce which receipts supported the period's cash total and which) Tj
T*
(items were excluded or unresolved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(DISTRIBUTABLE CASH) Tj
T*
(Begin with period collections plus the opening unrestricted cash balance. Exclude money) Tj
T*
(held in the tax escrow and exclude unreceived sale proceeds. A signed equipment sale) Tj
T*
(contract is not collected cash. Restricted reserve cash is separate from the opening) Tj
T*
(unrestricted balance and is not added a second time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX B | OPENING BALANCE RECONCILIATION) Tj
T*
(The opening unrestricted cash balance is traced to the previous period's signed closing) Tj
T*
(position and subsequent authorized adjustments. A draft distribution proposal is not a) Tj
T*
(signed closing position. If the prior period retained cash, the reconciliation identifies) Tj
T*
(where that cash remained and why it is not also described as a new collection. The same) Tj
T*
(amount must not enter the present worksheet once as opening cash and again as a current) Tj
T*
(receipt.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A book entry correcting an earlier classification is supported by an explanation and the) Tj
T*
(relevant source record. Staff do not assume every unexplained difference is distributable) Tj
T*
(simply because it appears in a cash account report. Restricted balances, unresolved) Tj
T*
(receipts and amounts belonging to another vehicle can appear in operational views that were) Tj
T*
(not designed to be distribution statements. The reviewer checks the meaning of the fields) Tj
T*
(before using their totals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The handover pack retains both the original prior-period report and the authorized) Tj
T*
(correction, when a correction exists. This makes a later change understandable without) Tj
T*
(pretending that staff had always reported the corrected number. A reconciliation can) Tj
T*
(explain an accounting difference; it does not by itself grant a new right to distribute) Tj
T*
(restricted money. The governing cash and reserve definitions remain the ones in the main) Tj
T*
(memorandum.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
