(NORMAL WATERFALL) Tj
T*
(Apply distributable cash in this order: \(1\) trustee fee, capped at 5 each period; \(2\)) Tj
T*
(senior current interest and senior interest arrears; \(3\) refill the liquidity reserve to) Tj
T*
(its target; \(4\) junior current interest; \(5\) any residual to the junior capital account. An) Tj
T*
(unpaid fee above the cap is not moved into senior interest. Unpaid senior interest carries) Tj
T*
(forward without interest on interest.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX C | TAX ESCROW SEPARATION) Tj
T*
(The tax escrow ledger is maintained separately from the unrestricted operating ledger.) Tj
T*
(Staff identify transfers into the escrow, authorized tax payments from it and any) Tj
T*
(unresolved tax reconciliation item. An escrow balance may be shown in an overall custody) Tj
T*
(report for completeness, but its inclusion in that report does not make it part of) Tj
T*
(distributable cash. The distribution analyst checks the account purpose as well as the) Tj
T*
(currency and balance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A tax invoice and a completed escrow payment are different records. The invoice can explain) Tj
T*
(a liability while the movement establishes that money was used. If a payment is made from) Tj
T*
(escrow, the analyst does not deduct it again from an unrelated unrestricted collection) Tj
T*
(total unless there is a distinct supported transaction. Double recording an escrow use can) Tj
T*
(understate cash just as adding escrow to the waterfall can overstate it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This appendix provides no investor tax rate or personal withholding rule. Operational staff) Tj
T*
(must not derive such a rate by dividing an escrow balance by a convenient receipt amount.) Tj
T*
(The escrow was established for its documented purpose and may relate to more than one) Tj
T*
(timing item. Investor tax questions require the separate applicable terms and records,) Tj
T*
(which are outside this fictional memorandum. A distribution calculation cannot create) Tj
T*
(missing tax instructions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX D | EQUIPMENT SALE STATUS) Tj
T*
(The asset manager tracks offers, signed sale contracts, delivery arrangements, invoiced) Tj
T*
(proceeds and actual collected proceeds as different stages. A signed sale contract may) Tj
T*
(justify a forecast in the planning report while leaving current distributable cash) Tj
T*
(unchanged until funds are received. The asset manager's estimate of the final resale value) Tj
T*
(is not a bank balance and should not be inserted into the present distribution to avoid a) Tj
T*
(projected shortfall.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If a purchaser pays an installment, staff match the actual receipt to the sale file and) Tj
T*
(retain the remaining amount as outstanding. The whole contract amount is not treated as) Tj
T*
(collected merely because one installment arrived. A deposit subject to a restriction is) Tj
T*
(classified under its actual terms instead of being assumed unrestricted. The cash analyst) Tj
T*
(requests clarification when a sale summary omits the status or restrictions associated with) Tj
T*
(an amount.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Canceled sales and returned deposits remain visible in the asset history. Staff do not) Tj
T*
(delete the old contract simply because it is no longer expected to complete. The archive) Tj
T*
(explains which receipts, refunds or unresolved claims resulted from it. None of these) Tj
T*
(operational events supplies a forecast equipment price for the exercise in the main) Tj
T*
(memorandum. That exercise is a closed snapshot and remains separate from the additional) Tj
T*
(casebook's hypothetical workflow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
