(RESERVE TARGET) Tj
T*
(The target is 40 while the performance trigger is clear. It becomes 70 when the trigger is) Tj
T*
(active. A refill uses the difference between the current reserve balance and the applicable) Tj
T*
(target, with a floor of zero. A reserve already above target does not pay a negative) Tj
T*
(refill; excess reserve is released only by a separately authorized release instruction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX F | SENIOR INTEREST REGISTER) Tj
T*
(The senior register distinguishes current interest, carried interest arrears and capital) Tj
T*
(balance. Staff trace each item to its relevant period and source record. A capital amount) Tj
T*
(cannot be inserted into the current interest line to accelerate a capital payment, and a) Tj
T*
(requested trustee fee cannot be entered as senior arrears. The headings are business) Tj
T*
(definitions, not free-form labels selected to obtain a preferred priority.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When previous senior interest was not paid, the arrears record carries the unpaid amount) Tj
T*
(forward under the main memorandum's treatment. The analyst retains the earlier signed) Tj
T*
(distribution notice to explain that amount. A planning spreadsheet may calculate) Tj
T*
(hypothetical future amounts, but those projections do not turn into actual arrears before) Tj
T*
(the relevant obligation arises. Reviewers compare both the amount and the obligation's) Tj
T*
(identity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The interest register is reconciled after payment using actual execution evidence. An) Tj
T*
(approved payment that fails at the bank remains distinguishable from a completed) Tj
T*
(distribution. If the next worksheet uses a revised arrears position, the file explains the) Tj
T*
(failed or corrected movement. Staff should be able to reconstruct the register without) Tj
T*
(adding interest on unpaid interest where the main terms do not permit it. A spreadsheet's) Tj
T*
(automatic compounding function is not independent contractual authority.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(PERFORMANCE TRIGGER) Tj
T*
(The trigger becomes active when the three-month average delinquency ratio is strictly above) Tj
T*
(4.0%. A value exactly 4.0% does not activate it. While active, junior current interest and) Tj
T*
(junior residual distributions are suspended; cash left after steps 1 through 3 remains in) Tj
T*
(unrestricted cash. Junior unpaid current interest is recorded, but does not jump ahead of) Tj
T*
(the reserve in the next period.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX G | LIQUIDITY RESERVE MOVEMENTS) Tj
T*
(The reserve ledger identifies its opening balance, authorized draws, refills and separately) Tj
T*
(authorized releases. The ledger is not a second copy of unrestricted cash. Staff check) Tj
T*
(movement direction and account purpose when reconciling it, because a transfer into reserve) Tj
T*
(reduces available unrestricted money while raising reserve. Listing the transfer as both a) Tj
T*
(new collection and a refill would count the same movement twice in different roles.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A proposed reserve release remains a proposal until its separate authority is present. A) Tj
T*
(worksheet can show an amount above the ordinary target without establishing that the) Tj
T*
(surplus has been released. Likewise, the restoration of a lower target after cure does not) Tj
T*
(itself prove that a bank transfer occurred. The archive separates the target calculation,) Tj
T*
(approval to release and actual execution evidence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When a draw has been authorized for a permitted current senior shortfall, the subsequent) Tj
T*
(refill uses the actual reduced reserve balance under the main sequence. Staff do not carry) Tj
T*
(the pre-draw balance into the refill calculation merely because it appeared in an earlier) Tj
T*
(draft. The records explain which balance was current at each step. This operational) Tj
T*
(guidance does not broaden the permitted draw purposes or permit junior interest, arrears or) Tj
T*
(fees to be funded from reserve.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
