(APPENDIX H | DELINQUENCY DATA PREPARATION) Tj
T*
(The servicer's delinquency file is prepared from the observation records used for the) Tj
T*
(performance test. Staff retain the observations, the source dates and the calculation) Tj
T*
(supporting the reported average. A rounded presentation in a management slide does not) Tj
T*
(automatically replace the underlying test input. The analyst checks whether a label) Tj
T*
(describes a monthly observation, a three-month average or a projection before applying the) Tj
T*
(main trigger condition.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A data correction is recorded with its reason and source. For example, a receipt assigned) Tj
T*
(to the wrong equipment reference can distort the delinquency file even while total bank) Tj
T*
(cash remains correct. Correcting that assignment may change a performance measure without) Tj
T*
(creating any new collection. Cash reconciliation and performance measurement must therefore) Tj
T*
(be reviewed together but cannot be treated as interchangeable tests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The file identifies which observations were used for a decision and preserves later) Tj
T*
(corrections separately. Staff cannot establish cure by selecting a favorable observation) Tj
T*
(and omitting an unfavorable intervening record. The main memorandum's) Tj
T*
(consecutive-observation condition continues to govern. A forecast that the average may) Tj
T*
(decline is planning information, not an observation date on which the performance trigger) Tj
T*
(has actually cleared.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(DISTRIBUTION EXERCISE) Tj
T*
(Period collections are 140, opening unrestricted cash is 10, and tax escrow is 20. A signed) Tj
T*
(but unpaid sale is 30. The reserve balance is 15. The trustee requests 7 in fees, senior) Tj
T*
(current interest is 50, senior interest arrears are 10, and junior current interest is 25.) Tj
T*
(The three-month delinquency average is 4.2%. No reserve release instruction exists and no) Tj
T*
(other deductions apply.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX I | TRIGGER STATUS REGISTER) Tj
T*
(The status register records when the performance trigger became active, which observations) Tj
T*
(supported that state and whether the cure test has subsequently been met. It should not) Tj
T*
(simply copy a green or red symbol from a presentation without the associated dates and) Tj
T*
(meaning. An active state and a new activation test are related but distinct questions;) Tj
T*
(staff must preserve the history needed to distinguish them.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For each distribution, the preparer links the state used in the worksheet to the relevant) Tj
T*
(status record. An old worksheet may show the trigger clear because it belonged to an) Tj
T*
(earlier period. Copying that worksheet's formatting into a new period does not establish) Tj
T*
(that the new period is clear. The reviewer checks the underlying observations and the state) Tj
T*
(transition, not merely the color or wording in a reused template.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When a disputed data item affects the status, the distribution file documents the) Tj
T*
(unresolved issue and the applicable decision process. This appendix does not invent a) Tj
T*
(waiver or permit a clerk to choose the state that gives a desired junior payment.) Tj
T*
(Historical status records remain available after cure so an auditor can understand why a) Tj
T*
(previous distribution was retained. Cure is a recorded condition under the main terms, not) Tj
T*
(a retroactive declaration that no trigger ever existed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
