(REPORTING REVIEW) Tj
T*
(The distribution notice should list cash available, each applied step, the ending reserve) Tj
T*
(and retained unrestricted cash. Amounts withheld from junior distribution are not a payment) Tj
T*
(to senior capital unless a separate capital repayment step is authorized. Staff should) Tj
T*
(retain the unapproved draft and the signed final notice with different version labels. A) Tj
T*
(reviewer may correct a transcription error before signing, but cannot move a restricted) Tj
T*
(escrow balance into the waterfall to make a draft reconcile. The cap applies to the current) Tj
T*
(trustee fee step; a requested fee above the cap is not permission to skip reserve) Tj
T*
(replenishment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX J | JUNIOR PAYMENT AND RETAINED CASH) Tj
T*
(The junior ledger separately tracks current interest, recorded unpaid junior interest and) Tj
T*
(amounts allocated to the junior capital account when the main sequence permits. A withheld) Tj
T*
(junior payment is not a completed distribution. It also does not automatically become) Tj
T*
(senior arrears or a repayment of senior capital. Staff preserve the obligation's class when) Tj
T*
(recording why money was not distributed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(While the trigger is active, the notice explains the retained unrestricted cash after the) Tj
T*
(permitted earlier steps. That retained balance should be identifiable in the closing cash) Tj
T*
(reconciliation and the next period's opening position. A narrative calling it reserved for) Tj
T*
(junior is not a completed transfer and does not create an automatic release instruction.) Tj
T*
(The cash remains classified according to the actual terms and recorded movements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Junior investors may ask why a period with positive collections did not produce a junior) Tj
T*
(payment. The explanation points to the applicable state, the earlier priority steps and the) Tj
T*
(retained cash, rather than describing collections as guaranteed return. Staff do not invent) Tj
T*
(a future payment date or promise a yield from one period's worksheet. The main memorandum) Tj
T*
(determines the current distribution, and later distributions require their own) Tj
T*
(observations, cash position and approvals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
