(CURE AND RELEASE) Tj
T*
(An active trigger clears only after the three-month average is at or below 3.0% on two) Tj
T*
(consecutive monthly observation dates. One low month is insufficient. After cure, the) Tj
T*
(ordinary target of 40 applies, but any release of reserve above 40 still needs the separate) Tj
T*
(release instruction. Cure alone does not turn previously suspended junior interest into) Tj
T*
(senior arrears.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX K | DRAW REQUEST PACKET) Tj
T*
(A reserve draw request identifies the specific current senior interest shortfall and shows) Tj
T*
(the cash position after the trustee fee step. The packet includes the source interest) Tj
T*
(register and the reserve balance available for review. A general statement that the trust) Tj
T*
(needs liquidity is insufficient to establish the permitted purpose. The reviewer checks the) Tj
T*
(requested use instead of assuming that any senior-labeled amount may be funded.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The two required approvals are recorded as distinct decisions with the packet version each) Tj
T*
(reviewer considered. A preparer cannot copy one approval into the other role's field. If) Tj
T*
(the packet changes materially after an approval, staff identify the change and obtain the) Tj
T*
(necessary review of the revised packet. The presence of a signature somewhere in the folder) Tj
T*
(is not enough to show that the final instruction was approved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Execution evidence is linked to the authorized request, and the reserve ledger is updated) Tj
T*
(to reflect the actual movement. A canceled or rejected instruction remains visible but does) Tj
T*
(not reduce reserve as though money had left. The later refill calculation uses the) Tj
T*
(supported balance. The operational packet makes the draw reproducible without adding new) Tj
T*
(authorized purposes, dispensing with either approval or treating reserve money as new) Tj
T*
(period collections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX L | DRAFT DISTRIBUTION WORKSHEETS) Tj
T*
(Preparers may create several draft worksheets while reconciling an input discrepancy. Each) Tj
T*
(draft is labeled with its source snapshot and review status. A draft is useful working) Tj
T*
(material, but its existence does not establish a payment obligation different from the main) Tj
T*
(memorandum. The final signed worksheet identifies the actual inputs and supersedes the) Tj
T*
(draft for execution without deleting the earlier working history.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The reviewer checks formulas and business definitions together. A spreadsheet can add rows) Tj
T*
(correctly while using tax escrow as unrestricted cash or placing a junior amount ahead of) Tj
T*
(reserve. Conversely, a formula error can produce the wrong amount even when the preparer) Tj
T*
(selected the correct class of inputs. Review comments describe which problem occurred so) Tj
T*
(the correction addresses its cause rather than simply replacing the final cell with a) Tj
T*
(desired number.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Hidden rows, stale links and copied period labels are reviewed as potential sources of) Tj
T*
(discrepancy. A locked workbook does not prove that its formulas are correct. The final) Tj
T*
(allocation should be reproducible from the source cash, obligations, reserve state and) Tj
T*
(trigger state using the stated order. Staff retain the review conclusion and corrected) Tj
T*
(version, allowing later examination of both the accounting result and the evidence) Tj
T*
(supporting it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(RESERVE DRAW) Tj
T*
(A liquidity draw may cover a shortfall in senior current interest only, after the trustee) Tj
T*
(fee step. It cannot pay junior interest, senior interest arrears, or fees. The draw) Tj
T*
(requires both trustee and oversight officer approval. A draw reduces the reserve balance) Tj
T*
(used in the later refill step; it is not new period collections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
