(APPENDIX M | DISTRIBUTION NOTICE DELIVERY) Tj
T*
(The signed distribution notice states the period, applied cash total, allocations, reserve) Tj
T*
(movements and retained balance relevant to that decision. The notice is delivered through) Tj
T*
(the recorded channel with a copy preserved in the archive. A draft sent for discussion is) Tj
T*
(labeled draft so recipients do not reasonably confuse it with the execution notice. Staff) Tj
T*
(should be able to identify which notice was final without reading an informal conversation) Tj
T*
(thread.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Where a transcription error is discovered after dispatch, the correction identifies the) Tj
T*
(prior notice and the specific change. Staff check whether the error was only in the) Tj
T*
(presentation or also affected an executed payment. These are different consequences and) Tj
T*
(require different supporting records. A corrected notice cannot by itself reverse a) Tj
T*
(completed bank movement; any actual correction must be traceable through its own authorized) Tj
T*
(instruction and execution evidence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The delivery log establishes what was sent and when, while the bank file establishes what) Tj
T*
(was paid. Neither substitutes for the other. A recipient's acknowledgement does not prove) Tj
T*
(that funds reached the recipient account, and a bank movement does not prove that all) Tj
T*
(disclosures in a notice were complete. The archive keeps both kinds of evidence so) Tj
T*
(operational completion can be assessed without turning a communication event into a) Tj
T*
(fictitious cash movement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(VERSION REGISTER) Tj
T*
(CE-8 released every residual to junior even when the trigger was active. CE-9 retains that) Tj
T*
(residual in unrestricted cash. The new rule applies to distribution periods ending on or) Tj
T*
(after 2026-09-01, including assets originated under CE-8. It does not reopen already) Tj
T*
(completed earlier distributions. Reserve targets and the cure test are unchanged.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(APPENDIX N | ASSET TRANSFERS AND ORIGINATION HISTORY) Tj
T*
(Equipment assets can have origination records created under an earlier operational edition.) Tj
T*
(The asset history explains the underlying leases and service arrangements, but it does not) Tj
T*
(independently choose the distribution rule for a later period. Staff distinguish the) Tj
T*
(asset's origination date from the ending date of the distribution period when applying the) Tj
T*
(transition provision in the main memorandum.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A file transfer between service teams preserves the original source documents and their) Tj
T*
(dates. Copying an asset folder into a newly named directory is not a new origination event,) Tj
T*
(and scanning an old agreement does not alter its execution date. Equally, old asset) Tj
T*
(identifiers do not preserve a superseded residual distribution treatment for every future) Tj
T*
(period. The preparer records the applicable edition and the event that makes it applicable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Completed historical distributions are retained as historical decisions. Staff do not) Tj
T*
(reopen them merely to make all archived notices use the same format or current terminology.) Tj
T*
(If a genuine correction is required, it is recorded as a correction with its basis, rather) Tj
T*
(than disguising a new worksheet as the original. The transition analysis needs both) Tj
T*
(business chronology and document identity; a filename prefix or software modification date) Tj
T*
(cannot replace either.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(BOUNDARY) Tj
T*
(This memorandum contains no actual borrower identities, a tax withholding rate for) Tj
T*
(investors, or a projected equipment sale price. The fictional amounts do not establish an) Tj
T*
(investment yield, and a cash-flow calculation cannot supply missing tax terms.) Tj
